From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:08:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: QMX CPU
 backstops

Add passive trips at 95 C (5 C hysteresis, 250 ms passive polling) on the
eight qmx-* zones, mapped to the cluster's CPU cooling device, next to the
cpu-* / cpullc-* backstops of the shell zone commit. The idea and the zone set
follow Doctor Logix's kaanapali-cpu-cooling.dtsi (denialwm 8bd03159587a),
which throttles the Pad 4 at 90 C; we keep our 95 C.

Promoted to the default device tree after the q91e opt-in rows passed
(7 Nov 2026, owner rule: what passes becomes the default).

Suggested-by: Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
Based-on: denialwm/linux-perpetua 8bd03159587a (zone set; the 95 C value is ours)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 .../kaanapali-oneplus-iceland-qmx-optin.dtsi  | 159 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts    |   1 +
 2 files changed, 160 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland-qmx-optin.dtsi

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland-qmx-optin.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland-qmx-optin.dtsi
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..b272ea8cc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland-qmx-optin.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
+/*
+ * OPT-IN, rehearsal only (q91d, 7 Nov 2026): CPU passive backstops on the eight QMX sensors, as Doctor Logix's
+ * kaanapali-cpu-cooling.dtsi (denialwm 8bd03159587a) does for every kaanapali board, with our value: 95 C and
+ * 5 C hysteresis, the same as the cpu-* / cpullc-* backstops of kaanapali-oneplus-iceland-thermal-optin.dtsi
+ * (denialwm uses 90 C on the Pad 4). Stock throttles at 105 C.
+ */
+
+&{/thermal-zones/qmx-0-0-thermal} {
+	polling-delay-passive = <250>;
+
+	trips {
+		qmx_0_0_backstop: qmx-0-0-backstop {
+			temperature = <95000>;
+			hysteresis = <5000>;
+			type = "passive";
+		};
+	};
+
+	cooling-maps {
+		map-backstop {
+			trip = <&qmx_0_0_backstop>;
+			cooling-device = <&cpu0 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&{/thermal-zones/qmx-0-1-thermal} {
+	polling-delay-passive = <250>;
+
